# Try the people endpoints by hand, using VS Code's REST Client extension or Visual Studio.
#
# They need an access token for a Family.Admin, read from a git-ignored file so it never
# sits in this tracked file (this repo is public):
#
#   1. Sign in to the web app, open the browser's dev tools, go to Network, click the `me`
#      request, and copy the value after "Bearer " in its Authorization header.
#   2. Put it in src/FamilyTree.Api/.env, next to this file, as one line:
#      FAMILYTREE_TOKEN=<the token>
#
# It lasts about an hour. Use fictional people here for now.

#@api = http://localhost:5080
@api = https://api.family.andrewmacleod.com
@token = {{$dotenv FAMILYTREE_TOKEN}}

### Add a person
POST {{api}}/api/v1/admin/people
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sex": "Female",
  "names": [
    { "givenName": "Isla", "surname": "Campbell", "type": "Birth" },
    { "givenName": "Isla", "surname": "MacLeod", "type": "Married" }
  ]
}

### List people, a page at a time
GET {{api}}/api/v1/admin/people?skip=0&take=50
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Read one person: replace the ID with one from the list
GET {{api}}/api/v1/admin/people/01a191bb-71f7-7816-930b-25f3daecd1a9
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Refused: a person needs a given name
POST {{api}}/api/v1/admin/people
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "names": [{ "surname": "MacLeod" }] }
